From d8fab95b9311158538de1418cb563037f278f6d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:02:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dynarmic: guarded links for indirect branches through a GOT
 slot (A64 on under Auto/Unsafe)

A block that ends in BR or BLR to a value it loaded from a constant address (a PLT stub's
LDR X17, [X16, #off]; BR X17, a call through the GOT) reads that slot as it is when the block is
translated (PeekCode, no side effects), compares the loaded value with it at the block's end
(FuseCheckBit tests the difference in its register) and links straight to that value's block when
they're equal; the fast dispatch lookup when not. Only canonical, 4-aligned, non-zero values; not
when the block sets FPCR or single-steps.

The A32 form (an ARM-state block ending in BXWritePC of a load from a constant address, LDR PC,
[IP, #off]!) is implemented behind A32::UserConfig::guarded_indirect_links but not turned on yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W5pLthrq7391gS4qodPV4u
